# Version / development documents (kept locally, not committed)
docs/versions/*
!docs/versions/*_results.md

# Generated run artifacts: ignore everything under data/ (runs, eval, the working tree) EXCEPT the
# secured tree, which is re-included by the two negations below. The negations are kept deliberately.
# `data/*` matches only one level down, and because data/secured_data/ already holds tracked files
# git descends into it regardless — so the secured tree is tracked today only through an interaction
# between this ignore pattern and the index, not through anything this file states. The two negations
# make the intent explicit, so the tracking of data/secured_data/ does not rest on that accident
# (06_workflow §6.3: a bold row whose checkpoint is not in the repository is a claim the repository
# cannot back). Secured snapshots and frozen pools carry SHA-256 pins in their ADOPTED.md manifests
# as the integrity mechanism. `!data/secured_data/` re-includes the directory; `!data/secured_data/**`
# re-includes its contents recursively (both lines are needed — the directory negation alone does not
# un-ignore the files beneath it).
data/*
!data/secured_data/
!data/secured_data/**

# Close-out tooling: the manifest + staging script that BUILD the commit, not artifacts of it.
.close_tooling/
tests/
scripts/analysis/
scripts/deck/

# Personal notes: local-only, never pushed.
docs/personal/
